



                         STAR TREK INSTRUCTIONS


  You will be assigned a starting point somewhere in the galaxy to serve
as commander of a starship. Your mission is to seek and destroy a fleet
of Klingon warships that have invaded and are menacing The United Federation
of Planets.

  The galaxy is divided into an 8x8 quadrant grid, and each quadrant is
further divided into an 8x8 sector grid. Quadrant 1,1 sector 1,1 is located
in the top left corner.

  You have the following commands available to you:

  imp - Impule Engines. These short range engines are typically used
        to manuever within a quadrant. You will be asked to give a
        course. The standard courses are in a range between 000 and 359.
        For example:

                 000
                  |
                  |
         270 --- <+> --- 090
                  |
                  |
                 180

        Next you will be asked to give an impulse factor. Each impulse
        factor equals one sector. So for example to move from sector
        5,5 to sector 5,4 you would select course 270 with an impulse
        factor of 1.


  srs - Short Range Sensors. Shows you a scan of your present quadrant.
     
        Symbology:

          <+> - Your Starship
          +K+ - Klingon Battle Cruiser
          >!< - Federation Starbase
           *  - Star

        A condensed status report is also presented.


  lrs - Long Range Sensors. 


	Shows conditions in space one quadrant on each side of
	the vessel, which is in the middle of the scan. The scan
	is coded in the form of \###\ where the units digit is
	the number of stars, the tens digit os the number of
	starbases, and the hundreds digit is the number of ships.

	For example:

          Long range sensor scan for quadrant 01, 07:

          |-----|-----|-----|
          | 000 | 000 | 000 |
          |-----|-----|-----|
          | 101 | 213 | 005 |
          |-----|-----|-----|
          | 005 | 002 | 005 |
          |-----|-----|-----|

	In quadrant 01, 07 the code is 213 which means there are
	2 ships (your ship, and one enemy), one station, and
	three stars. The 000 code is outside the known galaxy.

  pha - Phasers.

	Allows you to destroy enemy ships by zapping them with
	suitably large units of energy.

	Example:

          Energy Available: 3700

          Energy to Phasers: 100  <- You enter.

          60 unit hit on Klingon Battlecruiser at sector 5, 4


  tor - Photon Torpedoes

	A projectile weapon that travels a certain course to hit
	your enemy. Courses are the same as when navigating.
        After you fire a track will be displayed so you know
	where your torpedo went.

	Example:

          Torpedo Course: 270  <- You enter.

          Torpedo Track:
             3 8
             3 7
             3 6
             3 5
             3 4
             3 3
             3 2
             3 1
           Torpedo Missed


  she - Shield Control

        Defines the number of energy units to be assigned to the
	shields. Energy is taken from the ship's total energy.

	Example:

          Shield Control

          Energy Available for Shields = 4074

          Amount of energy to shields: 1000  <- You enter.

          Weapons Officer reports:
            Shields now at 1000 units per your command, sir.


  dam - Damage Control

	Gives the state of repair for all equipment. A
	status of less than 100 indicates damage.

	Example:

          Damage Control Report for Tiger:

            DEVICE               STATUS
          Impulse Engines         100
          Warp Engines            100
          Scanners                100
          Short Range Sensors     100
          Long Range Sensors       83
          Phasers                 100
          Photon Torpedoes        100
          Damage Control          100
          Shields                 100
          Library Computer        100


  wrp - Warp Engines

        Warp engines are exactly like impulse engines except that you
        move one whole quadrant instead of one whole sector per
        factor.

  com - Library Computer.

        Your onboard computer system. It has seven commands:

        cgr  - Cumulative Galactic Record. Shows computer memory
	       of all previous long and short range sensor scans.

        ddc  - Direction and Distance Calculator. Given two
	       locations will provide direction and distance
	       (speed required) to get there.

        exit - Exit Computer.

        loc  - Location Calculator. Given a location, course, and
	       speed, will provide new location.

        nav  - Starbase Navigation Data. Gives a recommended
	       course and speed to dock your ship.

        sta  - Status Report. Provides a detailed status report
	       of your situation and performance.

        tor  - Torpedo Course Calculator. Gives a recommended
	       course to aim torpedos.

  Good Luck!


